From 72c3efbd9488d0ecf78b6e4918d9add56eafc099 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Ornaghi Antunes <gustavo.ornaghiantunes@windriver.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:44:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Report and kill who is using DRBD device
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This patch includes code to report who is using the DRBD device when the
"drbdadm secondary..." command is executed.

The goal of this fix is to make debugging DRBD issues easier.

It also kills, as a last resort, the pod sandbox that holds the DRBD device
when "drbdadm secondary" still fails with "Device is held open by someone".
The holder is resolved from the container id in the cgroup path via
"crictl inspect" and the sandbox is removed with crictl (stopp/rmp) with up
to 3 retries, as no Kubernetes API is available during swact. After the kill
attempt the device is re-checked and a status is returned so the OCF flow can
decide instead of blindly retrying.

Signed-off-by: Gustavo Ornaghi Antunes <gustavo.ornaghiantunes@windriver.com>
Signed-off-by: Ítalo Vieira <italo.gomesvieira@windriver.com>
Signed-off-by: Pedro Trevisan <pedro.trevisan@windriver.com>
Signed-off-by: Arthur Santana Pedra <Arthur.SantanaPedra@windriver.com>
Signed-off-by: Edson CS <edson.coelhodossantos@windriver.com>
---
